                <pb facs="0749" n="629" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg629"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Italy/170: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Italy (Garrett)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-03-26T14:00:00-05:00">March 26, 1932—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. Department’s circular February 26th, 11 A.M. Treasury draft of agreement to
                    carry out Congressional Resolution regarding debt postponement has been handed
                    to Italian Ambassador today. Treasury anxious to expedite action. Department
                    does not desire that you make special call on officials regarding this but in
                    connection with other matters hopes you will find opportunity to inquire whether
                    prompt action can be expected.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
